cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CANIS: laptop-safe comparative canid genomics"
type: software
message: "If you use CANIS, please cite the software and the source datasets listed in the run report."
authors:
  - family-names: Kuhn
    given-names: Bennett
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-08-17
repository-code: "https://github.com/bennettek99-spec/canidgenomicspipeline"
url: "https://github.com/bennettek99-spec/canidgenomicspipeline"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  CANIS is a configuration-driven comparative evolutionary-genomics pipeline for
  canids. It emphasizes reproducible provenance, enforced quality control,
  laptop-safe execution, and explicit limitations for exploratory analyses.
keywords:
  - canids
  - comparative genomics
  - population genetics
  - introgression
  - reproducible research
